    "if you want a control option for the review discussion. Need live tuning?": "wenn Sie eine Kontrollmöglichkeit für das Rezensionsgespräch wünschen. Benötigen Sie Live-Tuning?",
    "in downtown Chicago. The conference is planned to begin Friday mid- to late afternoon and end Sunday by early afternoon. Final timing and venue details will be confirmed here.": "in der Innenstadt von Chicago. Die Konferenz soll am Freitag in der Mitte bis zum späten Nachmittag beginnen und am Sonntag am frühen Nachmittag enden. Der endgültige Zeitplan und die Einzelheiten zum Veranstaltungsort werden hier bestätigt.",
    "info@cureEDMD.org": "info@cureEDMD.org",
    "is Professor of Medicine and Pathology and Cell Biology at Columbia University and Attending Physician at New York-Presbyterian Hospital Columbia University Irving Medical Center. Dr. Worman received his BA from Cornell University and MD from the University of Chicago. He did an internship and residency in internal medicine at New York Hospital-Cornell Medical Center and a postdoctoral research fellowship in cell biology at Rockefeller University, where he started his research on the nuclear envelope.": "ist Professor für Medizin, Pathologie und Zellbiologie an der Columbia University und behandelnder Arzt am Irving Medical Center des New York-Presbyterian Hospital der Columbia University. Dr. Worman erhielt seinen BA von der Cornell University und seinen MD von der University of Chicago. Er absolvierte ein Praktikum und eine Facharztausbildung in der Inneren Medizin am New York Hospital-Cornell Medical Center sowie ein Postdoktorandenstipendium in Zellbiologie an der Rockefeller University, wo er mit seiner Forschung zur Kernhülle begann.",
    "is a professor in the Meinig School of Biomedical Engineering and the Weill Institute for Cell and Molecular Biology at Cornell University. He was appointed as the Associate Director of the Meinig School of Biomedical Engineering in 2024. He obtained a Diplom Ingenieur degree in Mechanical Engineering in his native Germany and a Bachelor of Engineering degree from the Thayer School of Engineering at Dartmouth College. Subsequently, he completed his Ph.D. in Biological Engineering at the Massachusetts Institute of Technology studying subcellular biomechanics and mechanotransduction signaling with Drs. Roger Kamm and Richard T. Lee (Brigham and Women’s Hospital/Harvard Medical School). Following a brief postdoctoral fellowship in Dr. Lee’s laboratory, he started his faculty career at Harvard Medical School/Brigham and Women’s Hospital while also teaching in the Department of Biological Engineering at the Massachusetts Institute for Technology before joining Cornell University in 2011.": "ist Professor an der Meinig School of Biomedical Engineering und am Weill Institute for Cell and Molecular Biology der Cornell University. Im Jahr 2024 wurde er zum stellvertretenden Direktor der Meinig School of Biomedical Engineering ernannt. In seinem Heimatland Deutschland erwarb er einen Diplom-Ingenieur-Abschluss in Maschinenbau und einen Bachelor of Engineering an der Thayer School of Engineering am Dartmouth College. Anschließend schloss er seinen Ph.D. ab. in Biological Engineering am Massachusetts Institute of Technology, wo er bei Dr. subzelluläre Biomechanik und Mechanotransduktionssignalisierung studiert. Roger Kamm und Richard T. Lee (Brigham and Women’s Hospital/Harvard Medical School). Nach einem kurzen Postdoktorandenstipendium in Dr. Lees Labor begann er seine Fakultätslaufbahn an der Harvard Medical School/Brigham and Women’s Hospital und lehrte gleichzeitig am Department of Biological Engineering am Massachusetts Institute for Technology, bevor er 2011 an die Cornell University wechselte.",
