    "Lori L. Wallrath, PhD": "洛里·L·瓦尔拉斯博士",
    "Lori Wallrath develops fruit-fly models carrying patient-associated lamin mutations to investigate skeletal-muscle and cardiac laminopathies. Her models have revealed abnormalities in nuclear organization, nucleo-cytoskeletal coupling, oxidative stress, protein aggregation, and muscle function, creating a tractable system for testing genetic and pharmacological modifiers. She also contributed to the influential 2020 study showing that mutant lamins cause mechanically induced nuclear-envelope rupture and DNA damage in skeletal muscle. Her work is particularly valuable because it connects fundamental lamin biology with rapid in vivo screening for potentially modifiable disease pathways.": "Lori Wallrath 开发了携带患者相关核纤层蛋白突变的果蝇模型，以研究骨骼肌和心脏核纤层蛋白病。她的模型揭示了核组织、核细胞骨架耦合、氧化应激、蛋白质聚集和肌肉功能的异常，创建了一个用于测试遗传和药理学修饰剂的易于处理的系统。她还为 2020 年颇具影响力的研究做出了贡献，该研究表明突变核纤层蛋白会导致机械诱导的核膜破裂和骨骼肌 DNA 损伤。她的工作特别有价值，因为它将基本的核纤层蛋白生物学与快速体内筛选潜在可改变的疾病途径联系起来。",
    "Lori Wallrath, University of Iowa": "洛里·瓦尔拉斯，爱荷华大学",
    "Luisa Mestroni is a major leader in the genetics of familial dilated cardiomyopathy and directs the International Familial Cardiomyopathy Registry. Her program connects disease-gene discovery with longitudinal patient follow-up, arrhythmia risk, heart failure, and experimental treatment. Her LMNA-related translational work helped bring inhibition of the p38 MAPK pathway into phase 2 clinical testing with ARRY-371797, moving a mechanism first identified in laboratory models into studies involving patients. Whether or not a particular therapy ultimately succeeds, this bench-to-clinic pathway is an important model for future EDMD drug development.": "Luisa Mestroni 是家族性扩张型心肌病遗传学领域的主要领导者，也是国际家族性心肌病登记处的负责人。她的项目将疾病基因发现与患者纵向随访、心律失常风险、心力衰竭和实验性治疗联系起来。她的 LMNA 相关转化工作帮助 ARRY-371797 将 p38 MAPK 通路的抑制带入 2 期临床测试，将实验室模型中首次发现的机制转移到涉及患者的研究中。无论特定疗法最终是否成功，这种从实验室到临床的途径都是未来 EDMD 药物开发的重要模型。",
    "Luisa Mestroni, MD": "路易莎·梅斯特罗尼，医学博士",
