    "Ann Schmidt": "アン・シュミット",
    "Ann Schmidt, MS, CGC": "アン・シュミット、MS、CGC",
    "Ann is a board-certified genetic counselor with more than 25 years of experience spanning pediatric genetics, hereditary cancer genetics, telehealth, genomic policy, genetics payment integrity, and clinical billing integrity. Throughout her career, Ann has been committed to helping patients and families understand complex genetic information and navigate their healthcare journeys. Her passion for rare disease advocacy extends beyond her professional work through volunteering with the Wisconsin Rare Disease Alliance and cureEDMD. She believes that listening to patients and families and building a connected, informed community are essential to advancing research and improving the lives of those affected by EDMD.": "アンは、小児遺伝学、遺伝性がん遺伝学、遠隔医療、ゲノム政策、遺伝学の支払いの完全性、および臨床請求の完全性にわたる 25 年以上の経験を持つ、委員会認定の遺伝カウンセラーです。アンはそのキャリアを通じて、患者と家族が複雑な遺伝情報を理解し、医療への道を歩めるよう支援することに尽力してきました。希少疾患の擁護に対する彼女の情熱は、ウィスコンシン希少疾患アライアンスやcureEDMDでのボランティア活動を通じて、専門的な仕事を超えて広がっています。研究を進め、EDMD の影響を受ける人々の生活を改善するには、患者と家族の声に耳を傾け、情報に基づいたつながりのあるコミュニティを構築することが不可欠であると彼女は信じています。",
    "Another approach would be to try to develop a new drug that addresses targets identified in EDMD. This could include targets downstream of the implicated genes themselves. This might have a higher probability of success than searching for existing drugs that are effective, but it is very costly (probably $10 million or more) and most likely very time consuming, on the order of several years at least even with sufficient funding. cureEDMD intends to seek or help motivate such funding once reasonably high-probability disease targets are identified.": "別のアプローチは、EDMD で特定された標的に対処する新薬の開発を試みることです。これには、関与する遺伝子自体の下流の標的が含まれる可能性があります。 This might have a higher probability of success than searching for existing drugs that are effective, but it is very costly (probably $10 million or more) and most likely very time consuming, on the order of several years at least even with sufficient funding. ureEDMD は、かなり確率の高い疾患の標的が特定されたら、そのような資金提供の動機付けを模索または支援する予定です。",
    "Antoine Muchir was the lead experimental investigator on the influential study identifying early MAPK activation in an LMNA EDMD model. His subsequent work showed that pharmacologic inhibition of pathways such as ERK and JNK could reduce fibrosis, improve cardiac function, or delay cardiomyopathy in experimental models. These studies provided some of the earliest evidence that a molecular pathway downstream of lamin dysfunction could be therapeutically targeted. His group continues to investigate signaling, calcium regulation, fibrosis, and other modifiable mechanisms in striated-muscle laminopathies.": "Antoine Muchir は、LMNA EDMD モデルにおける初期の MAPK 活性化を特定する影響力のある研究の実験研究責任者でした。 His subsequent work showed that pharmacologic inhibition of pathways such as ERK and JNK could reduce fibrosis, improve cardiac function, or delay cardiomyopathy in experimental models.これらの研究は、ラミン機能不全の下流の分子経路が治療の標的になり得るという最も初期の証拠の一部を提供した。彼のグループは、横紋筋椎弓障害におけるシグナル伝達、カルシウム制御、線維症、およびその他の修正可能なメカニズムの研究を続けています。",
    "Antoine Muchir, Institute Myology, France": "アントワーヌ・ムチル、ミオロジー研究所、フランス",
    "Antoine Muchir, PhD": "アントワーヌ・ムチル博士",
    "April 2–4, 2027 · Chicago, Illinois": "2027 年 4 月 2 ～ 4 日 · イリノイ州シカゴ",
    "April 2–4, 2027 · Downtown Chicago": "2027 年 4 月 2 ～ 4 日 · シカゴのダウンタウン",
    "Arrhythmia prediction, heart failure, cardiac surveillance, and patient registries": "不整脈の予測、心不全、心臓の監視、患者登録",
    "As of 2026, there is no cure for EDMD, and care focuses on symptom management. Treatment may include cardiology care, medications, pacemakers, implanted defibrillators (CRT-D), physical therapy, and contracture management.": "2026年の時点ではEDMDの治療法はなく、治療は症状の管理に重点が置かれています。治療には、心臓病治療、投薬、ペースメーカー、植込み型除細動器 (CRT-D)、理学療法、拘縮管理などが含まれる場合があります。",
    "Asia-Pacific": "アジア太平洋地域",
    "At a young age, EDMD may first appear as muscle weakness and stiff elbows or ankles, often with toe walking. After the teenage years and into early adulthood, heart problems may become more common.": "若い年齢では、EDMD は最初に筋力低下と肘や足首の硬直として現れることがあり、多くの場合つま先歩きを伴います。 10代を過ぎて成人初期になると、心臓の問題がより一般的になる可能性があります。",
